					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/adam-henderson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1350867); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1350867&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973924" alt="Adam Henderson" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1350867)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/adam-henderson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1350867); return false;" >Adam Henderson</a></span> <span class="odate time_1340454944 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">23 Jun 2012 12:35</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1487980">
									

<p>While I like your report, you forgot two big reasons why a HE civilization would want to invade.</p>
<p><strong>To convert us to their religion/s.</strong></p>
<p>Look at <em>human</em> history. Repeatedly we have a culture getting invaded by another culture with the goal of religious conversion. Perhaps the HE culture would be the equivalents of missionaries or crusaders, out to convert/kill if they don't convert the heretic humans.</p>
<p>Sure it makes no sense, but considering humans have repeatedly done it who's to say a HE would be smarter.</p>
<p><strong>To get their hands/tentacles/claws/whatever onto SCP items.</strong></p>
<p>We have loads of odd stuff which could presumably be useful. Who's to say that the HE wouldn't be here to take stuff to use in their civilization? Or for such reasons as to rescue their lost astronaut, SCP-163? Or as revenge via planet-killer kinetic energy weapons to those horrible monsters, SCP-1000 and what they did back when they had a HE level culture of their own&#8230;. Pity about the time limitations of interstellar travel meaning that SCP-1000 culture is gone now&#8230;.</p>

							</div>

								
					
