			<div class="content" id="post-content-1488052">
									

<p>Yeah, I was thinking about the same things. I too see at least two reason why Aliens could bother invading anyway:</p>
<p><strong>The Covenant Approach:</strong> They are on a grand crusade to unite all life under their belief system, and Humanity just happens to be the next race on their list. This makes being able to eat us or bang us irrelevant.</p>
<p><strong>The Combine Approach:</strong> Though biologically incompatible with our biosphere themselves, they are still willing to govern us through subservient augmented trans-human proxies. Afterwards, since the law of physics are universal, they can still communicate and rule through the interstellar equivalent of the internet, and put us to work to manufacture goods for export and mine resources in our solar system.</p>
<p>Still, this is an excellent and very well informed article.</p>

