														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1488455">
									

<p>Definitely something that Project Heimdall needs to have in its files. Though I'd posit that, well, maybe the aliens are just assholes. Even if there's no particular -use- in doing something, sometimes people (and presumably aliens) just want to watch the other guy's world burn.</p>
<p>There's also what I hesitantly term the &quot;Psychlo Reasoning&quot;, in that Earth happens to have an abundance of some useful natural resource that there is a dearth of on the aliens' home planet(s). (In Battlefield Earth, they wanted our gold, though presumably an HE covered under Project Heimdall would want something a little less insipid.) This could even simply be the raw materials for something else that they're after; perhaps the aliens came from a cyanide-based ecosystem but have discovered that they can create useful materials or desirable luxuries out of oxygen. That would also be a reason to enslave; they get to (for the most part) stay on their environmentally-sealed ships and domes while the humans work in the &quot;hostile&quot; environment making whatever desired object they came here for.</p>
<p>And, as a corollary to what Adam Henderson said, what if there's an HE whose mindset works similar to the GOC? They could view us as infidels for not destroying these dangerous objects, or even believe us to be allied with some of the sapient ones like, say, 682. That would be a reason to desire to overturn us, maybe even punish us under their version of a judicial system.</p>
<p>&#8230; the possibilities for this are fascinating, aren't they?</p>

							</div>

								
					
