<blockquote>
<p>in that Earth happens to have an abundance of some useful natural resource that there is a dearth of on the aliens' home planet(s).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>From a geological standpoint, the composition of the various other balls of rock in our solar system are fairly equivalent. For that matter, mining the asteroid belt would be <em>far</em> more lucrative than mining Earth. Realistically speaking, if it's resources that you're after (fossil fuels notwithstanding - and even then I'm pretty sure there are complex hydrocarbons present in the local gas giants), go mine a lifeless ball of rock that doesn't have feisty natives.</p>

